			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CLAMP\nThe Clamp node makes sure that the incoming value stays within its min and max values. When the input is lower than the min, the min is sent out. When the input is higher than the max, the max is sent out. If the value is within the range the value is sent out without alterations.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• The Sine produces a value running from -0.5 to 0.5 and back.\n• This value modulates the Y position of the yellow circle.\n•.The value of the sine also gets clamped between -0.2 and 0.2 before modulating the Y of the blue circle.\n• Even though the sine outputs values above -0.2 and 0.2 the clamp makes sure it stays within range, acting as hard stops for the circle.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 269.9287109375,
					"width": 910.38360595703125,
